1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,640
That's a big old moose print right there.
那里有个很大的驼鹿脚印。

2
00:00:03,640 --> 00:00:06,401
The whole place stinks of rotten salmon.
整个地方都有腐烂鲑鱼的臭味。

3
00:00:06,401 --> 00:00:14,000
It's a smell I associate with the fall.
这是一种我会联想到秋天的气味。

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,280
Wherever there's salmon there's usually bears.
哪里有鲑鱼，通常就有熊。

5
00:00:17,280 --> 00:00:24,281
There's lots of salmon on the beach.
这片沙滩上有很多鲑鱼。

6
00:00:24,281 --> 00:00:34,961
Well I didn't bring a tent with me so I'm looking for places to build a shelter tonight.
我没带帐篷，所以在找今晚可以搭建庇护所的地方。

7
00:00:34,961 --> 00:00:38,521
Look at that it's a small black bear print.
看那里，是一个小黑熊的脚印。

8
00:00:38,521 --> 00:00:43,360
That's his front pad right there there's his toes and his claws.
那是它前脚的肉垫，那里是脚趾和爪痕。

9
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:46,881
See this that's a bald eagle print right there.
看到这个了吗？那里是白头海雕的脚印。

10
00:00:46,881 --> 00:00:52,881
You can see his talons you see he walked all over here.
你可以看到它的利爪印，看，它在这一带走来走去。

11
00:00:52,881 --> 00:00:57,841
It's a wolf print he went down here and came back.
那是狼的脚印，它往这边走了，又回来了。

12
00:00:57,841 --> 00:01:02,400
The print of a little fox right there.
那里是一只小狐狸的脚印。

13
00:01:02,400 --> 00:01:09,400
A couple coyote prints there that right there and there.
那里有几个郊狼脚印，就在那儿和那儿。

14
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:13,040
All the animals are walking the beach looking for salmon.
这些动物都沿着沙滩走，寻找鲑鱼。

15
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:18,361
Nothing but stinking fish now though.
不过现在只剩下发臭的鱼了。

16
00:01:19,400 --> 00:01:29,320
I see a few spots that could work as shelters in a pinch but I'm going to keep looking.
我看到了几个紧急情况下可以当庇护所的地方，不过我还要继续找。

17
00:01:29,320 --> 00:01:32,321
Yeah that wouldn't be a bad spot to get out of the rain.
嗯，那里用来躲雨倒也不错。

18
00:01:32,321 --> 00:01:48,281
I'm kind of liking this spot there's lots of wood around for fire and building materials.
我有点喜欢这个地方，周围有很多可以生火和搭建用的木头。

19
00:01:57,800 --> 00:02:13,041
Man I've been using this saw for 3 years now two years now thing's done good.
天哪，这把锯子我用了三年了——现在算两年吧，一直挺好用。

20
00:02:13,041 --> 00:02:16,401
Tell you what this is a beautiful spot on a beautiful day.
跟你说，这么美的一天，待在这么美的地方真好。

21
00:02:16,401 --> 00:02:19,880
And it's tempting to try to just sleep out under the the stars.
让人很想干脆在星空下露宿。

22
00:02:19,880 --> 00:02:22,800
But it's going to get cold bitterly cold tonight.
但是天气会冷下来，今晚会非常寒冷。

23
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:29,111
The low is supposed to be around 20 f but there's a stiff cold wind coming off that lake.
预计最低气温在华氏二十度左右，而且湖面上吹来一股强劲的冷风。

24
00:02:29,121 --> 00:02:32,281
Luckily that hill shelters us a little bit.
幸好，那座小山给我们挡了一点风。

25
00:02:32,281 --> 00:02:35,880
If you go just 100 ft that way the wind is just in your teeth.
如果再往那边走一百英尺，风就直接扑面而来。

26
00:02:35,880 --> 00:02:48,201
So the most important thing my shelter can do is block that wind.
所以，这个庇护所最重要的作用就是挡住那股风。

27
00:03:48,041 --> 00:03:50,481
All right I got a nice little shelter here.
好了，我这里有个不错的小庇护所。

28
00:03:50,481 --> 00:03:54,481
Got this natural awning that'll keep the frost and rain off me.
这个天然的遮檐能帮我挡住霜和雨。

29
00:03:54,481 --> 00:03:59,421
Got this wind break up I think it's time to build a fire and make some lunch.
挡风的部分也搭好了，我想该生火做午饭了。
